  <Fragment slot="content">
    <section class="date-time-content">
      <h2>Date & Time Calculator – Calculate Time, Work Hours and Date Differences</h2>
      <p>
        The <strong>Date & Time Calculator</strong> is a versatile multi-function utility designed to solve all everyday, professional, timesheet, payroll, and logistics time calculations. This comprehensive suite includes dedicated modules for <strong>adding and subtracting time</strong>, <strong>calculating work hours and shifts with breaks</strong>, <strong>measuring elapsed time between two times or dates</strong>, <strong>converting durations to decimal hours</strong>, and <strong>estimating USPS delivery dates</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2>What Is a Time Calculator?</h2>
      <p>
        A <strong>time calculator</strong> performs mathematical operations on chronological units — days, hours, minutes, and seconds — which operate on a base-60 (sexagesimal) numbering system rather than standard base-10 decimals.
      </p>
      <p>
        Because there are 60 seconds in a minute, 60 minutes in an hour, and 24 hours in a day, standard decimal calculators frequently produce errors when adding or subtracting time. A dedicated time calculator handles borrowing and carrying automatically.
      </p>

      <h2>How to Use This Date and Time Calculator</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Select Calculation Mode:</strong> Use the top mode switcher to pick Time Calculator, Work Time, Elapsed Time, Date Difference, or USPS Delivery.</li>
        <li><strong>Enter Required Values:</strong> Input your hours, minutes, starting timestamps, or calendar dates.</li>
        <li><strong>Click Calculate:</strong> Press the blue <strong>"Calculate →"</strong> button or hit <kbd class="px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-slate-200 dark:bg-slate-800 font-mono text-xs">Enter</kbd> to reveal the result.</li>
        <li><strong>Review Detailed Breakdown:</strong> Check the normalized hours/minutes format, decimal hours for payroll, or working days count.</li>
        <li><strong>Use Clear:</strong> Click <strong>"Clear (✕)"</strong> anytime to reset the active calculator.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Add Time Calculator</h2>
      <p>
        The <strong>Add Time Calculator</strong> allows you to combine multiple durations. When the sum of seconds reaches 60, it increments the minutes by 1; when minutes reach 60, it increments the hours by 1.
      </p>
      <div class="my-4 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-100/80 p-4 font-mono text-sm dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
        <div class="font-bold text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">Example Addition:</div>
        <div class="mt-1">2 Hours 45 Minutes 30 Seconds  +  1 Hour 30 Minutes 45 Seconds</div>
        <div class="mt-1">= 3 Hours 75 Minutes 75 Seconds  ➔  4 Hours 16 Minutes 15 Seconds (4.27 decimal hrs)</div>
      </div>

      <h2>How to Subtract Time</h2>
      <p>
        Subtracting time requires borrowing 60 units from the higher denomination whenever the subtrahend exceeds the minuend:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>If subtracting <code>45 seconds</code> from <code>10 seconds</code>, borrow 1 minute (60 seconds) to make it <code>70 seconds - 45 seconds = 25 seconds</code>.</li>
        <li>If subtracting <code>50 minutes</code> from <code>20 minutes</code>, borrow 1 hour (60 minutes) to make it <code>80 minutes - 50 minutes = 30 minutes</code>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Work Time Calculator & Timesheet Payroll</h2>
      <p>
        The <strong>Work Time Calculator</strong> calculates net billable hours for employees and freelancers:
      </p>
      <div class="my-4 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-100/80 p-4 font-mono text-sm dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
        <div class="font-bold text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">Work Hours Formula:</div>
        <div class="mt-1">Net Work Duration = End Time - Start Time - Unpaid Breaks</div>
      </div>
      <p>
        <strong>Overnight Shifts:</strong> When a shift begins at night (e.g., 10:00 PM) and finishes the next morning (e.g., 6:00 AM), our calculator automatically detects the midnight rollover to compute the exact 8-hour gross duration.
      </p>

      <h2>Time Calculator Between Two Times</h2>
      <p>
        Quickly determine the duration between any two clock times (e.g., <code>9:30 AM to 5:45 PM = 8 Hours 15 Minutes = 8.25 Hours</code>).
      </p>

      <h2>Time Calculator in Hours (Decimal Time Conversion)</h2>
      <p>
        Payroll systems require time in decimal hours rather than hours and minutes:
        <br />
        <code>Decimal Hours = Hours + (Minutes ÷ 60) + (Seconds ÷ 3600)</code>.
        <br />
        For example: <strong>7 Hours and 45 Minutes = 7 + (45 ÷ 60) = 7.75 Hours</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2>Elapsed Time Calculator</h2>
      <p>
        The <strong>elapsed time calculator</strong> measures the exact duration between two full date-and-time timestamps, taking leap years, varying month lengths (28 to 31 days), and clock times into account.
      </p>

      <h2>Date Difference Calculator & Working Business Days</h2>
      <p>
        The <strong>Date Difference Calculator</strong> counts total elapsed calendar days between two dates, while separating <strong>Monday-to-Friday business working days</strong> from weekends. You can also customize the active working days checklist (e.g. for 6-day work weeks).
      </p>

      <h2>Date and Time Calculator (Add Duration to Date)</h2>
      <p>
        Compute target deadlines by adding or subtracting years, months, weeks, days, hours, and minutes from any starting date (e.g. <code>Sep 1, 2026 10:30 AM + 2 Days 5 Hours 30 Mins = Sep 3, 2026 4:00 PM</code>).
      </p>

      <h2>USPS Delivery Time Calculator</h2>
      <p>
        Estimates package arrival windows for eCommerce shipments based on handling time and standard USPS transit estimates:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>USPS Ground Advantage:</strong> 2 to 5 business days.</li>
        <li><strong>USPS Priority Mail:</strong> 1 to 3 business days.</li>
        <li><strong>USPS Priority Mail Express:</strong> 1 to 2 days (overnight guarantee on select routes).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <em>Disclaimer:</em> Delivery estimates are non-guaranteed approximations for planning purposes.
      </p>

      <h2>Common Time Formulas Reference</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto my-4">
        <table class="min-w-full text-left text-xs sm:text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-900">
              <th class="py-3 px-3 font-bold">Operation</th>
              <th class="py-3 px-3 font-bold">Mathematical Formula</th>
              <th class="py-3 px-3 font-bold">Example</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100 dark:divide-slate-800">
            <tr><td class="py-2.5 px-3 font-semibold">Minutes to Hours</td><td class="py-2.5 px-3"><code>Minutes ÷ 60</code></td><td class="py-2.5 px-3">90 mins = 1.5 hrs</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="py-2.5 px-3 font-semibold">Seconds to Hours</td><td class="py-2.5 px-3"><code>Seconds ÷ 3600</code></td><td class="py-2.5 px-3">7200 s = 2 hrs</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="py-2.5 px-3 font-semibold">Days to Hours</td><td class="py-2.5 px-3"><code>Days × 24</code></td><td class="py-2.5 px-3">3 days = 72 hrs</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="py-2.5 px-3 font-semibold">Net Work Time</td><td class="py-2.5 px-3"><code>End - Start - Break</code></td><td class="py-2.5 px-3">9am to 5pm (30m brk) = 7.5 hrs</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2>Time Conversion Tables</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto my-4">
        <table class="min-w-full text-left text-xs sm:text-sm">
